  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef wants to construct two special strings SSS and TTT of length NNN using only characters AAA, BBB, and CCC for a coding challenge. Both strings must satisfy:\n\n\nNo two adjacent characters are the same.\nTheir Longest Common Subsequence is exactly KKK.\nChef needs your help to determine if it's possible to construct such strings SSS and TTT. If it's possible, output the strings; otherwise, output −1-1−1.\n\n**Note:**\n\n\nGiven two sequences (or strings), the Longest Common Subsequence is the longest sequence that can be derived from both original sequences by deleting some (or no) elements without changing the order of the remaining elements. Unlike substrings, the characters of a subsequence do not need to occupy consecutive positions.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, If possible, print SSS and TTT each on a new line; otherwise, print −1-1−1.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N≤10001 \\leq N \\leq 10001≤N≤1000",
      "0≤K≤N0 \\leq K \\leq N0≤K≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 100010001000."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 0\n3 0\n3 3\n4 3",
        "output": "A\nB\n-1\nABC\nABC\nABCA\nACBA",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: LCS(A,B)=0LCS(A, B) = 0LCS(A,B)=0.\nTest Case 2: It can be proved that there are no such possible strings.\nTest Case 3: LCS(ABC,ABC)=3LCS(ABC, ABC) = 3LCS(ABC,ABC)=3.\nTest Case 4: LCS(ABCA,ACBA)=3LCS(ABCA, ACBA) = 3LCS(ABCA,ACBA)=3."
      }
    ]
  },
